# Modal backdrops — keep the host screen readable

## Hard rule
When a modal / sheet / overlay opens, the **background UI must stay clearly visible**.
Do **not** blur or heavily darken the host screen.

## Approved backdrop
Shared pattern (already on `.settings-backdrop` / `.facility-backdrop` and stage prep/info backdrops):

```css
background: #07050c44; /* light dim only */
backdrop-filter: none;
-webkit-backdrop-filter: none;
```

Prefer the shared class `.settings-backdrop` (or the matching facility/stage backdrop class) instead of inventing a new opaque scrim.

## Disallowed
```css
backdrop-filter: blur(...);
-webkit-backdrop-filter: blur(...);
background: #000a;      /* too opaque */
background: #07050ccc;  /* too dark */
```

Do not reintroduce per-modal “strong dim + blur” overrides for shop, mission, community, power-up, skill-feed, settings, or similar sheets.

## Checklist for new modals
1. Use `.settings-backdrop` (or an existing shared backdrop class).
2. No `backdrop-filter` / `-webkit-backdrop-filter` blur on the scrim.
3. Dim stays light (`#07050c44` or equivalent ~25% opacity).
4. Soft open/close still follows soft-modals (no full `render()` just to toggle the overlay).
